From 1130ab466eb32cb86f9ce7c8f95d054a3ec3d0eb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suiyan <suiyan@sunmmio.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 16:06:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?target/dadao:=20picolibc=20backend=20enablement?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20=E2=80=94=20mem*=20expand,=20varargs,=20indirect=20call=20(M?=
 =?UTF-8?q?L-003a-d)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Real-C libc compilation (picolibc) exercised codegen paths never hit by
hand-written test vectors, surfacing and fixing a cluster of backend gaps:

- llvm.memcpy/memmove/memset intrinsics: force full inline expansion
  (MaxStoresPerMem* = UINT_MAX) since brcond-based expansion was
  previously unselectable.
- varargs (VASTART): DADAOMachineFunctionInfo (VarArgsFrameIndex/Size) +
  DADAOTargetMachine::createMachineFunctionInfo override — printf's
  va_list handling no longer null-derefs.
- GPRB spill/reload support in storeRegToStackSlot/loadRegFromStackSlot.
- Jump tables (BR_JT/BRIND/JumpTable) + ConstantPool addressing, with
  AsmPrinter MO_JumpTableIndex/MO_ConstantPoolIndex lowering — unlocks
  switch statements and float/double literal pooling.
- CTTZ/CTLZ/CTPOP set to Expand.
- Function-pointer indirect calls (previously deferred, DL-063b/c):
  CALL_PSEUDO_INDIRECT (DADAOInstrInfo.td) + expandPostRAPseudo case,
  dispatched via DAGToDAG only when the DADAOISD::CALL callee is a
  plain register (not GlobalAddress/ExternalSymbol, which keep the
  existing direct CALL_IIII construction — binding tglobaladdr/
  texternalsym as a Pat<> operand on the chain+glue call node trips a
  scheduler BuildSchedUnits assertion regardless of Pseudo-ness).
  Ground-truth repro matrix (7 cases spanning global/local callee,
  void/int return, 0/const/variable args) all pass; picolibc's
  libc/stdio/vfprintf.c (the real trigger — tinystdio's FILE dispatches
  through function-pointer put/get callbacks) now compiles.
- Fixed an adjacent latent segfault: the direct-call path unconditionally
  built a 3-operand {Callee, Chain, Glue} list even when Glue is absent
  (0 register arguments), crashing createOperands on the null SDValue —
  mirrors the conditional-push already used on the indirect-call path.

Verified: 27/27 E2E, differential AGREE(4-way)=200/DIVERGE=0, no
regression on existing direct calls.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
